// CACHE: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits | owner=CodeEditorLand | repo=Sky | per_page=5 | page=36 → GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits.RESPONSE.map(Author,Date,File,Message,SHA)
{
	"Set": [
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T23:39:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				142,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Sky): Remove IPv6 localhost allowance from Content Security Policy\n\nRevert the inclusion of `http://[::1]:*` in the CSP `connect-src` directive across all editor entry points (Browser, BrowserProxy, Electron, Mountain, and index). The recent addition of the 127.0.0.1 wildcard rule (`http://127.0.0.1:*`) already satisfies the requirement to allow connections to the local OTLP exporter (port 4318) when `Inspect` is enabled.\n\nThe duplicate IPv6 allowance was unnecessary given the specific localhost configuration of the Tauri dev server and could potentially broaden the attack surface on platforms where IPv6 loopback resolution behaves inconsistently. This ensures a minimal and secure CSP definition while maintaining full functionality for local tracing and inspection.",
			"SHA": "c92f48a856787975e50c335a1ee641dcd04ce88f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T23:05:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				142,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add retry logic for Tauri IPC bridge initialization\n\nReplace the immediate-exit check for `__TAURI__` globals in `Source/Workbench/Bundled/Electron/Layout.astro` with a 5-second polling loop. The previous implementation failed to find the invoke handle during race conditions between ES-module execution and Wry's content-script injection, causing lifecycle phase advances to be silently dropped and leaving the editor unable to invoke Mountain actions (Open Folder, dialogs, terminal).\n\nIntroduce `ResolveInvoke` and `WaitForInvoke` to bridge the gap across two specific race scenarios: module evaluation outpacing bridge injection and differing `window.__TAURI__` namespace structures in forked Tauri builds. On failure, emit a specific console error and a `land:bundled:electron:tauri-missing` performance mark; on success, log `land:bundled:electron:tauri-resolved`.\n\nEnsure `lifecycle:advancePhase(3)` reliably triggers upon webview restoration, preventing the \"Sky did not advance to Restored within 8s\" log spam and enabling immediate interaction with native OS features.",
			"SHA": "ce9eea79f1ba8c22ae40e5c082b25932e5aec4ea"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T22:59:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
